Z||000000||Sophia Nova||11-05-2001||09:43 AM||||Quick question...I am planning on putting a 350 in my 88 Fiero, but I'm not sure how I should go about it.  Can I just have a regular mechanic do the swap, or should I trail on down to Archie's?  What would be the difference in cost/workmanship?<BR>Thanks!<BR>Sophia||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||11-05-2001||10:20 AM||||You should also direct this question to Archie specifically.  I know that Archie has finished tons of the V-8 Conversions (check the tech session... he's been doing a couple of play-by-plays lately).  So you can't go wrong having Archie do it.  If you feel that you have a competent mechanic, then maybe you can trust them to do it- I'd be weary though.  Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
